Prefix sum is nothing but a kind of array which contains the sum of all elements before that element.
The size of the given list is equal to the size of the prefix sum
nums = [1, 7, 3, 6, 5, 6]
Prefix sum array p is:
p[0] = nums[0] = 1
p[1] = nums[0] + nums[1] = 1+7 = 8
p[2] = nums[0] + nums[1] + nums[2] = 8+3 = 11
p[3] = 1+7+3+6 = 17
So the prefix sum array becomes:
p = [1, 8, 11, 17, 22, 28]

Method -2(Using prefix sum logic to find pivor index ):
class Solution:
    def pivotIndex(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:
        p=[]
        s=0
        for i in range(len(nums)):
            s+=nums[i]
            p.append(s)
        t=0
        for i in range(len(nums)):
            s-=nums[i]
            if s==t:
                return i
            t+=nums[i]
        else:
            return -1
